                <pb facs="0613" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg529"/>

                <head>No. 279.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">King Kaldkaua to the
                    President.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram received at the Executive Mansion from
                        San Francisco, Cal, October 2, 1886.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-09-25"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 25,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I desire to convey through you my heartfelt sympathy for the sufferers by the
                    great earthquakes which have devastated so many homes.</p>
                <closer><signed>KALAKAUA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
